The examples in this directory are described in the userguide.


Short description
-----------------

structures1:

 A simple truss problem (based on an example in the course Mechanics 4RA00).

structures2:

 A simple 3D truss problem.

structures3:

 A simple 1D cantilever beam problem 
 P3 interpolation

structures4:

 A simple 1D cantilever beam problem 
 P4 interpolation

structures5:

 A simply supported or built-in 1D beam problem
 P3 interpolation

structures6:

 A simple 1D cantilever beam problem 
 Function for distributive load.
 P4 interpolation

structures7:

 A simply supported or built-in 1D beam problem
 Different distributed load on parts of the beam using two groups of
 elements with difference coefficients. Alternatively a function can be
 defined for q.
 P3 interpolation

structures8:

 A left built-in 1D beam problem with optional supports.
 Different distributed load on parts of the beam using three groups of
 elements with difference coefficients.
 Alternatively a function can be defined for q.
 Forces and/or moments in all points.
 P3 interpolation

structures9:

 A left built-in 1D beam problem with optional supports.
 Different distributed load on parts of the beam using three groups of
 elements with difference coefficients.
 Alternatively a function can be defined for q.
 Forces and/or moments in all points.
 P1/P3 interpolation. 

 Identical to structures8, except using 2D elements instead of 1D elements.

structures9a:

 A left built-in 1D beam problem with optional supports.
 Different distributed load on parts of the beam using three groups of
 elements with difference coefficients.
 Alternatively a function can be defined for q.
 Forces and/or moments in all points.
 P1/P4 interpolation. 

 Identical to structures9, except using P1/P4 interpolation

structures10:

 A left built-in 2D beam problem with optional supports.
 Different distributed load on parts of the beam using three groups of
 elements with difference coefficients.
 Alternatively a function can be defined for q.
 Forces and/or moments in all points.
 P1/P3 interpolation. 2D elements.
 Similar to structures9 with the following extensions:
  - axial loading
  - optional angle with respect to the x-axis

structures10a:

 A left built-in 2D beam problem with optional supports.
 Different distributed load on parts of the beam using three groups of
 elements with difference coefficients.
 Alternatively a function can be defined for q.
 Forces and/or moments in all points.
 P2/P4 interpolation. 2D elements.
 Similar to structures9 with the following extensions:
  - axial loading
  - optional angle with respect to the x-axis

 Identical to structures10, except using P2/P4 interpolation

structures11:

 A two-beam structure problem. Gravity load.
 Forces and moment in point 2 (tip of triangle).
 P1/P3 interpolation. 2D elements.
 Gmsh mesh. 

structures11a:

 A two-beam structure problem. Gravity load.
 Forces and moment in point 2 (tip of triangle).
 P2/P4 interpolation. 2D elements.
 Gmsh mesh. 

 Identical to structures11, except using P2/P4 interpolation

structures12:

 A beam structure problem of exam Mechanics 8-11-2019. Gravity load.
 Forces in point 2 and 3. Builtin at point 1 and 5
 P1/P3 interpolation. 2D elements.
 Gmsh mesh. 

structures13:

 A simple 2D truss problem
 (question 1 of exam on 8-11-2019 of course Mechanics 4RA00).

structures14:

 A simple 2D truss problem with two groups having a different cross section.
 (interim exam on 23-09-2015 of course Mechanics 4RA00).

structures15:

 A simple 2D truss problem with two groups having a different cross section.

 Similar to structures14, but now includes gravity load (lumped to the nodes).

structures16:

 A two-beam structure problem. Gravity load. 3D beam elements.
 Forces and moments in point 2 (tip of triangle).
 Gmsh mesh. 
 P1/P3/P1 interpolation for axial displacement, transverse displacement
 and axial rotation, respectively.

 Extension of structures11 to a 3D beam structure.

structures16a:

 A two-beam structure problem. Gravity load. 3D beam elements.
 Forces and moments in point 2 (tip of triangle).
 Gmsh mesh. 
 P2/P4/P2 interpolation for axial displacement, transverse displacement
 and axial rotation, respectively.

 Identical to structures16, except using P2/P4/P2 interpolation.

structures17:

 A left built-in torsion shaft problem consisting of three parts. 3D beams.
 Different polar second moments of area on parts of the shaft
 using three groups of elements with difference coefficients.
 External torques moments in all points.
 P1/P3/P1 interpolation for axial displacement, transverse displacement
 and axial rotation, respectively.

structures18:

 A two-beam structure problem: an L-shaped wrench. 3D beam elements.
 A force down in point 3. Example from the Mechanics course 4RA00.
 Gmsh mesh. 
 P1/P3/P1 interpolation for axial displacement, transverse displacement
 and axial rotation, respectively.

structures19:

 A 3D cantilever beam problem with unsymmetric bending
 P1/P3/P1 interpolation for axial displacement, transverse displacement
 and axial rotation, respectively.

